### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Colección REST — flujos del módulo de RUIZ AKLE, JUAN
### Cubre: challenges, schemas, test-data y demo end-to-end.
### Compatible con VS Code REST Client e importable a Postman.
###
### Cómo usar:
###   1) docker compose up -d
###   2) Ejecutar la primera petición (login admin) para obtener un token.
###   3) Copiar el accessToken al @adminToken arriba.
###   4) Ejecutar las demás secciones en orden.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

@host = http://localhost:3000/api

# Tokens (rellenar tras login)
@adminToken = REEMPLAZAR_ADMIN_TOKEN
@profToken  = REEMPLAZAR_PROFESSOR_TOKEN
@studToken  = REEMPLAZAR_STUDENT_TOKEN

# IDs (rellenar a partir de respuestas)
@profId      = REEMPLAZAR_PROFESSOR_ID
@studId      = REEMPLAZAR_STUDENT_ID
@courseId    = REEMPLAZAR_COURSE_ID
@challengeId = REEMPLAZAR_CHALLENGE_ID

### =======================================================================
### 1. AUTH — login con el ADMIN seedeado
### =======================================================================

### 1.1 Login ADMIN (usar el accessToken como @adminToken)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 1.2 Crear PROFESSOR (ADMIN-only) — guardar id como @profId
POST {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Profe123!",
  "fullName": "Profesora Demo",
  "role": "PROFESSOR"
}

### 1.3 Crear STUDENT (ADMIN-only) — guardar id como @studId
POST {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "stud.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Stud123!",
  "fullName": "Estudiante Demo",
  "role": "STUDENT"
}

### 1.4 Login PROFESSOR (usar accessToken como @profToken)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Profe123!"
}

### 1.5 Login STUDENT (usar accessToken como @studToken)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "stud.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Stud123!"
}

### =======================================================================
### 2. DEMO end-to-end — atajo para sustentación
### Crea curso + reto publicado + esquema + dataset en una sola llamada.
### =======================================================================

### 2.1 Demo customers/orders (PROFESSOR)
POST {{host}}/demo/customers-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseName": "Demo BD2 2026",
  "courseCode": "DEMO-2026-1",
  "customerCount": 100,
  "orderCount": 1000
}

### =======================================================================
### 3. FLUJO MANUAL — desde cero (alternativa al demo)
### =======================================================================

### 3.1 Crear curso (PROFESSOR) — guardar id como @courseId
POST {{host}}/courses
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bases de Datos II",
  "code": "BD2-2026-1",
  "period": "2026-1",
  "group": "1"
}

### 3.2 Inscribir STUDENT en el curso (PROFESSOR del curso)
POST {{host}}/courses/{{courseId}}/enrollments
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "{{studId}}"
}

### 3.3 Crear reto SQL en draft — guardar id como @challengeId
POST {{host}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clientes con más de 3 compras",
  "description": "Construya una consulta SQL que retorne los clientes con más de 3 compras, ordenados por número de compras descendente.",
  "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
  "tags": ["SELECT", "JOIN", "GROUP BY", "HAVING"],
  "databaseEngine": "postgresql",
  "timeLimit": 2000,
  "courseId": "{{courseId}}"
}

### 3.4 Cargar esquema DDL (solo CREATE TABLE)
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/schema
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ddl": "CREATE TABLE customers (id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY, name VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL, city VARCHAR(60), tier VARCHAR(16), created_at DATE NOT NULL); CREATE TABLE orders (id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY, customer_id INT REFERENCES customers(id) NOT NULL, total DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL, status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL, currency VARCHAR(3) NOT NULL, created_at DATE NOT NULL);"
}

### 3.5 Consultar esquema cargado (incluye parsedTables con metadata rica)
GET {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/schema
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### 3.6 Preview del SQL generado (sin persistir)
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/test-data/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "preview_demo",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table": "customers",
      "rows": 5,
      "seed": 1,
      "fields": {
        "name": { "type": "varchar", "preset": "name", "maxLength": 80 },
        "city": { "type": "varchar", "preset": "city" },
        "tier": { "type": "enum", "values": ["BRONZE", "SILVER", "GOLD"], "weights": [50, 30, 20] },
        "created_at": { "type": "date", "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2026-12-31" }
      }
    }
  ]
}

### 3.7 Generar dataset (con casos borde + faker)
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/test-data/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "dataset_principal",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table": "customers",
      "rows": 100,
      "seed": 1,
      "fields": {
        "name": { "type": "varchar", "preset": "name", "maxLength": 80 },
        "city": { "type": "varchar", "preset": "city", "maxLength": 60 },
        "tier": { "type": "enum", "values": ["BRONZE", "SILVER", "GOLD"], "weights": [50, 30, 20] },
        "created_at": { "type": "date", "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2026-12-31" }
      }
    },
    {
      "table": "orders",
      "rows": 1000,
      "seed": 2,
      "fields": {
        "customer_id": { "type": "foreign_key", "references": "customers.id" },
        "total": { "type": "decimal", "min": 10000, "max": 5000000, "includeExtremes": true },
        "status": { "type": "enum", "values": ["PENDING", "PAID", "CANCELLED"], "weights": [10, 80, 10] },
        "currency": { "type": "varchar", "fixedValue": "COP" },
        "created_at": { "type": "date", "from": "2026-01-01", "to": "2026-12-31" }
      }
    }
  ]
}

### 3.8 Listar datasets del reto
GET {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/test-data
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### 3.9 Publicar reto (draft → published)
PATCH {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "published" }

### =======================================================================
### 4. STUDENT — vista filtrada por rol
### =======================================================================

### 4.1 STUDENT lista retos (solo published de cursos donde está inscrito)
GET {{host}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 4.2 STUDENT ve detalle del reto publicado (200)
GET {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### =======================================================================
### 5. CASOS BORDE / VALIDACIONES (deben fallar con 400/403/404)
### =======================================================================

### 5.1 STUDENT intenta ver un reto NO publicado → 404 (no leakea existencia)
###     Crear primero un reto en draft con 3.3 sin publicarlo, copiar su id.
GET {{host}}/challenges/REEMPLAZAR_DRAFT_CHALLENGE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 5.2 PROFESSOR intenta archivar reto con submissions activas → 400
PATCH {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "archived" }

### 5.3 DDL prohibido (DROP) → 400
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/schema
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ddl": "DROP TABLE customers;" }

### 5.4 DDL prohibido (ALTER) → 400
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/schema
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ddl": "ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN x INT;" }

### 5.5 Generador con min>max → 400
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/test-data/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "edge_case",
  "tables": [{
    "table": "x",
    "rows": 1,
    "fields": { "v": { "type": "integer", "min": 100, "max": 10 } }
  }]
}

### 5.6 Generador con weights mal alineado → 400
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/test-data/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "edge_case",
  "tables": [{
    "table": "x",
    "rows": 1,
    "fields": {
      "v": { "type": "enum", "values": ["A", "B"], "weights": [1, 2, 3] }
    }
  }]
}
